</address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINOHARA, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUZUKI, KENGO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINOHARA TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUZUKI KENGO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINOHARA, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUZUKI, KENGO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Minimum units for specifying the position and size of an effective area of an image transmitted from a camera are set irrespective of each other in order that the restriction on one of the minimum units does not influence the other. The minimum unit (I, J) for specifying the position of the effective area is determined to be a value separate from and independent of the minimum unit (C, D) for specifying the dimensions of the effective area. Therefore, even if there is restriction on one of the minimum units, the restriction does not influence the other.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Des unités minimales pour spécifier la position et la dimension d'une surface effective d'une image transmise depuis une caméra sont fixées indépendamment les unes des autres, afin que la restriction concernant l'une des unités minimales n'influe pas sur l'autre. L'unité minimale (I, J) destinée à spécifier la position de la surface effective est déterminée de manière à être une valeur séparée et indépendante de l'unité minimale (C, D) permettant de spécifier les dimensions de la surface effective. Par conséquent, même en cas de restriction sur une des unités minimales, cette restriction n'influe pas sur l'autre.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>